  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "After named gap-hardness/parallel-repetition and ordinary Fourier prerequisites, the proof must make virtual Hadamard subcodes cover the global code almost uniformly via the full Hellinger calculation at992–1098, and transfer local point-subspace acceptance to side-condition-respecting global Fourier lists at1123–1300. The composed proof at1303–1432 still has to identify shared virtual-table positions and convert those lists into consistent outer strategies while maintaining the q^6-alphabet and4/q soundness bounds. These complete new covering, local-to-global and composition obligations form one conservative H2 task above a direct PCP theorem invocation or routine Fourier exercise.",
  "source_scope_note": "Exact original Main Theorem1.2 only: for any fixed prime q>=5 and constant zeta>0, NP-hardness of distinguishing 2P1R games with R=q^6 answers and value at least1-zeta versus at most4/q. Full authored q/q^6 query-alphabet overview, projection/repetition and 3LIN definitions and named gap theorems, Fourier and Hellinger conventions, new repeated outer game and full subcode-covering calculation/parameters, complete Gowers and side-condition tests, point-subspace soundness proof and composed-PCP table identification/list-decoding closing are retained. Named Håstad 3LIN hardness, Raz-Holenstein-Rao parallel repetition, ordinary finite-field Fourier/Parseval, convexity and Hellinger inequalities are prerequisites; all new local covering, inner-test and composition material is supplied. Growing-field and quadratic-programming claims are unselected and uncounted. All-page source/output QA completed and exact final actual logs checked. Source-material candidate only; no admission/remote-delivery credit.",
  "source_quirks_note": "The original subcode parameter paragraph at1088 retains the negative exponent -Omega(beta k), whereas preceding authored bound at971 is positive Omega(beta k); both remain as printed. Native1056 retains the coefficient wording |a_2|=O(beta^2 q^2), and the overview452 retains its assignment codomain Phi. The original disjoint-equation high-probability/negligible exception at987–989 and1346–1348 is included verbatim, with no added padding, counterexample analysis or mathematical repair.",
